## Context

On PR 2365 (2026-11-09) gaze planned one other-family seat (codex,
gpt-6-luna). The seat read the tree and answered "No findings ... Verdict:
clear". Its second line was

    reach: read=yes shell=yes tests=not-run (read code only)

`scripts/gaze_seat.py:456` matches the reach line whole and allows nothing
after `tests=`, so `reach_refusal` answered "invalid reach declaration", the
report was discarded, the plan check failed, and the review was recorded
`seats: self-only` (raw id 20261109T225531Z-3921936; the report text was read
back from the codex session file).

How often: the history of `refs/notes/review` over the 7 days to 2026-11-10
holds 9 lines with "seat reach: invalid reach declaration", 6 on the codex
door with gpt-6-luna and 3 on the claude-code door with sonnet. One report
may appear in several lines; at least 2 are distinct by raw id, and raw ids
exist only since 2026-11-07.

The launch rails state the format and, in the same sentence, "ran tests or
read code only" (`scripts/gaze_seat.py:122-124`). The gloss the seat added
repeats those words.

History. Ticket 1290 (2026-10-27) introduced the line to refuse a seat that
could not read and to record whether tests ran. Commit 57343040 (2026-10-31)
already added one tolerance, for a header wrapped in a Markdown block. This
is the second round of format noise on the same check.

Why not a grammar: ticket 1378 put "a grammar on seat reports" out of scope
by author ruling, and ticket 1465 holds it, deferred until there is a
consumer need and evidence that each CLI door accepts a schema. A format
stated in the prompt is a request, which is what failed here. Probe of
2026-11-10, logged on 1465.

## Decisions for the plan

- Read the three fields from the reach line and ignore what follows them.
  Refuse what 1290 meant to refuse: no reach line, `read=no`, a repeated
  declaration. Do not add a second pattern for the next kind of noise.
- Keep the seat's line intact in the filed report.
- Show the seat one literal example line, and drop the wording that invites
  a gloss.
- Out of scope: passing a schema to the doors (ticket 1465).

## Test

In `tests/test_gaze_seat.py`, with the fake seat:
- a clear whose reach line ends with extra text is filed, line intact
  (red first: today it is "invalid reach declaration");
- `read=no` followed by extra text is still no report;
- the existing cases for a missing line and a repeated line pass unchanged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A report whose second line declares read, shell, and tests and then
  carries extra text is filed, with that line intact
- [ ] `read=no`, a missing reach line, and a repeated declaration are still
  no report
- [ ] The launch rails show one literal example line and no wording that
  invites a gloss
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Imagine (raid 6ee79f)

- **Premise check: holds.** `reach: read=yes shell=yes tests=not-run (read
  code only)` fails `REACH.fullmatch`, whose pattern ends `\s*$`
  (`scripts/gaze_seat.py:456`); the line starts `reach:`, so `reach_refusal`
  returns "invalid reach declaration" (`:467-468`) and the caller answers "no
  report" (`:501-502`). Nothing on main voids it.
- **Must keep** (`tests/test_gaze_seat.py`). A reader that ignored everything
  after `tests=` would accept `tests=ran=no` (case `fenced-ranno`, `:71`,
  expected refusal at `:996`). `read=maybe` (`:78`, `:997`) stays refused: the
  values stay exact. The late, missing, repeated, quoted, and example cases do
  not depend on trailing text. Rule: a tail starts only at whitespace or at
  the end of the line.
- **Simplest path.** Change the end of the one pattern at `:456` so that
  `tests=(ran|not-run)` may be followed by whitespace and any text. Both
  `fullmatch` calls (`:464`, `:470`) then behave as before, and the filed
  report keeps the seat's line. No helper, no second pattern.
- **Sites.** Rails (`scripts/gaze_seat.py:122-124`),
  `profiles/code-reviewer/PROFILE.md:29`,
  `profiles/prose-reviewer/PROFILE.md:25`,
  `skills/gaze/references/panel.md:54-56`. No copy under `adapters/`. For
  exit criterion 3 the rails must change; the two profiles repeat the same
  wording and reach the seat too, so align them in the same commit. The
  panel reference describes the meaning and can stay.
- **Verification without wording pins.** The behaviour tests of the Test
  section. Criterion 3 is read from the diff at review. No test pins the
  rails' wording today; add none.
- **Antipatterns.** None with the one-pattern change. Avoid: a second pattern
  for other noise, a tolerance helper, parsing the tail for meaning.
- **Later review.** Count "seat reach: invalid reach declaration" in
  `refs/notes/review` over the 7 days after the merge, against 9 before. A
  doctor journal revisit, no wait ticket.
- **Risk and coder.** Low; the one risk is a pattern that loosens
  `tests=ran=no`.

## Blind-spot pass (raid 6ee79f)

- `BLIND-SPOT: CLEAN` (gpt-6.1-sol, `codex exec`, read-only; id from the
  session header).
- Orchestrator check, not raised by either agent: the forms of the other
  refused lines. Of 342 raw seat outputs retained since 2026-11-07, 337 have
  a valid reach line, 3 a valid line followed by a parenthetical gloss, 2 no
  reach line in their first 12 lines, none any other malformed form. The
  one-pattern change covers every observed case.

## Plan (raid 6ee79f, written by the orchestrator)

- **Actions.** (1) `scripts/gaze_seat.py:456`: let `tests=(ran|not-run)` be
  followed by whitespace and any text, to the end of the line; update the
  docstring at `:460` if it no longer describes the rule. (2) Launch rails,
  `:122-124`: one literal example line; drop "ran tests or read code only".
  (3) `profiles/code-reviewer/PROFILE.md:29` and
  `profiles/prose-reviewer/PROFILE.md:25`: the same wording as the rails.
- **First test** (`tests/test_gaze_seat.py`, red first): a fake-seat mode
  whose second line is `reach: read=yes shell=yes tests=not-run (read code
  only)` followed by a clear; assert exit 0, the report filed, and the reach
  line present with its tail. Today it fails with "invalid reach
  declaration". Companion: `read=no` with a tail is still exit 1 with
  `read=no`. The parametrized refusals (`fenced-ranno`, `fenced-unknown`,
  repeated and late lines) stay as they are and must stay green: they are
  what catches a pattern loosened too far.
- **Not a test:** the wording of the rails and profiles (a wording pin).
- **Files.** `scripts/gaze_seat.py`, `tests/test_gaze_seat.py`, the two
  profiles. No registry, no `routes.json`.
- **Dependencies.** None. Open merge requests 2367 and 2370 touch none of
  these files (checked 2026-11-10).
- **Exit criteria map.** 1: action 1 and the first test. 2: the companion
  and the unchanged refusals. 3: actions 2 and 3, read at review. 4: the
  coder runs the gate.

